      "If pathogens get past the barriers, the innate immune response acts within minutes to hours. Damaged tissue releases chemical signals that cause inflammation, bringing more blood and white blood cells to the site. Phagocytes such as neutrophils and macrophages engulf and digest invaders. The innate response is fast but nonspecific: it reacts in much the same way to many different pathogens.",
